<p>a ball will fall. trade on where it lands.<p>I made this game! Some technical details:<p>The entire drop of the ball is simulated server-side, then streamed to each client as server-sent events with a small buffer. Every drop is deterministic from its starting position, so rounds can be replayed exactly for later analysis, but tiny variations in starting position can change the ultimate outcome.<p>There's some AI traders to keep the market moving, but they drop out in any round that has more than five people. They operate using a naive set of rules that I wrote for them, so they're not too hard to beat -- it's when the market is full of real people that it gets tricky.<p>Curious to get feedback on anything you would change, and especially whether the mechanics were clear right away or not.</p>
<hr>
